1
00:00:00,501 --> 00:00:03,921
Please welcome the woman
leading La Familia into the future.

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,924
The Nation's Chairmom, Diana Aragon.

3
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:09,301
There was food poisoning
at our feeding program

4
00:00:09,385 --> 00:00:10,511
in Corpuz City.

5
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:12,847
We're terminating our partnership,
effective immediately.

6
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:14,640
I need to get to the bottom of this!

7
00:00:14,724 --> 00:00:16,350
Give me answers!

8
00:00:17,059 --> 00:00:18,811
-Ms. D! Ms. D!
-Ms. D!

9
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:24,233
Code blue! Code blue!

10
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:32,908
What happened?

11
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:34,326
Why are you here?
You're not allowed in here.

12
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:35,911
-Uh…
-What happened?

13
00:00:35,995 --> 00:00:37,204
-Who are you?
-Ouch!

14
00:00:37,872 --> 00:00:39,039
What did you do to Ms. D?

15
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:40,958
Who are you?!

16
00:00:41,375 --> 00:00:42,501
Patricia?!

17
00:00:42,585 --> 00:00:43,961
Check the connections.

18
00:00:44,712 --> 00:00:45,713
There's a loose connection.

19
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:48,424
-I'll fix it, doctor.
-Okay. Please secure it.

20
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:50,050
-Let me check.
-All good, doctor.

21
00:01:53,989 --> 00:01:55,533
Who is it? Hold on!

22
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:56,742
Hold on!

23
00:01:56,826 --> 00:01:57,952
Stop pounding the door!

24
00:01:58,035 --> 00:01:59,620
What do you need?! Oh!

25
00:02:00,830 --> 00:02:02,039
How may I help you?

26
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:03,749
Seriously?

27
00:02:03,833 --> 00:02:06,919
You haven't paid the rent
for almost three months!

28
00:02:07,002 --> 00:02:09,338
You keep asking for extensions!

29
00:02:09,421 --> 00:02:10,965
You keep making empty promises!

30
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:12,716
Now, what? Still nothing!

31
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,677
Madam, of course, we'll pay the rent.

32
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,637
It's just that something
unexpected happened.

33
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,930
Maybe you can--

34
00:02:18,013 --> 00:02:20,015
No! This is business, Carlota!

35
00:02:20,099 --> 00:02:23,227
If you can't pay right now, then get out!

36
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:25,020
Maybe we can still talk about this.

37
00:02:25,104 --> 00:02:27,565
Let's just wait for Patricia to come home.

38
00:02:27,648 --> 00:02:29,525
She already emptied her savings!

39
00:02:29,608 --> 00:02:32,444
-Martin, give our money back!
-Get out!

40
00:02:32,528 --> 00:02:34,405
If you don't want
to get hurt, then pay up!

41
00:02:34,488 --> 00:02:36,156
Where's our money?!

42
00:02:37,908 --> 00:02:39,743
Vital signs are stable.

43
00:02:39,827 --> 00:02:41,370
It's just a connection problem.

44
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:44,915
Argh! What the hell!

45
00:02:44,999 --> 00:02:46,375
I told you I didn't do anything!

46
00:02:46,709 --> 00:02:47,793
Patricia.

47
00:02:49,545 --> 00:02:50,629
It's really you.

48
00:02:52,047 --> 00:02:52,882
Patricia?

49
00:03:00,973 --> 00:03:02,308
Let me just remind everyone

50
00:03:02,391 --> 00:03:04,393
that I'm not just a board member here,

51
00:03:04,476 --> 00:03:06,228
or a senior officer.

52
00:03:06,312 --> 00:03:07,813
I'm the only…

53
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:09,648
family member right now.

54
00:03:09,732 --> 00:03:13,360
La Familia exists because of our family.

55
00:03:13,444 --> 00:03:15,779
And I have the same access,

56
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:18,073
same values, and principles.

57
00:03:18,157 --> 00:03:21,035
And I have proven that
over the years of working here.

58
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:21,952
I agree.

59
00:03:22,036 --> 00:03:24,997
The majority of the board
has already decided

60
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,832
to appoint Teodor Aragon

61
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:29,251
for the interim leadership position.

62
00:03:29,335 --> 00:03:31,420
Well, thank you.

63
00:03:31,837 --> 00:03:33,881
I better start working, then.
Meeting adjourned.

64
00:03:44,266 --> 00:03:46,143
Hello, Georgia, my daughter.

65
00:03:47,770 --> 00:03:49,438
Guess who's the new CEO?

66
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:51,649
Dad!

67
00:03:52,441 --> 00:03:54,485
Something's happening here
in the hospital.

68
00:03:55,277 --> 00:03:56,403
What?

69
00:03:58,364 --> 00:03:59,573
Why are you looking at me like that?

70
00:04:01,075 --> 00:04:02,242
You really don't remember me?

71
00:04:03,202 --> 00:04:04,495
I'm Enzo.

72
00:04:05,496 --> 00:04:08,207
Lorenzo De Leon. Your childhood playmate.

73
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:09,333
Enzo?

74
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:12,544
-You work for Mom?
-Yes!

75
00:04:13,295 --> 00:04:14,588
I'm her Chief of Staff.

76
00:04:15,130 --> 00:04:17,716
But wait, what happened to you?

77
00:04:18,550 --> 00:04:20,010
I haven't seen you for a long time.

78
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:23,555
I heard someone's pretending
to be my sister's daughter.

79
00:04:23,639 --> 00:04:24,932
Where's that scammer?

80
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:28,102
She's not pretending, Sir Teddy.

81
00:04:35,150 --> 00:04:36,235
What are you doing here?

82
00:04:36,318 --> 00:04:38,237
Am I not supposed to be here?

83
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:41,657
Yes, but after all these years,
when Diana's in this condition,

84
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,826
now, you show up? What do you need? Money?

85
00:04:43,909 --> 00:04:47,079
I heard your dad wasted everything he got

86
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:48,288
from the annulment.

87
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:51,125
He invested in all
these failed businesses.

88
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:54,461
-Did he tell you to come here?
-Don't drag Dad into this.

89
00:04:54,545 --> 00:04:56,797
I just don't want Diana to be agitated.

90
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:59,883
What if she wakes up
and sees you first thing?

91
00:05:01,510 --> 00:05:02,594
So, tell me.

92
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,138
How much do you need?

93
00:05:05,973 --> 00:05:08,350
It's now or never!
Attorney, please explain it.

94
00:05:09,143 --> 00:05:12,438
Well, legally speaking,
you're not entitled to any inheritance

95
00:05:12,521 --> 00:05:13,897
while your mother is still alive.

96
00:05:14,648 --> 00:05:16,984
-I know.
-So you do know?

97
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:20,738
If you're scaring me with your lawyer…

98
00:05:21,822 --> 00:05:24,533
Article 777 of the Civil Code.

99
00:05:25,159 --> 00:05:27,619
The right to inheritance
is only transferred

100
00:05:27,703 --> 00:05:30,080
at the time of death of the heir.

101
00:05:30,164 --> 00:05:31,957
As long as the parent is still alive,

102
00:05:32,041 --> 00:05:36,003
they still have full ownership
of their assets.

103
00:05:36,086 --> 00:05:38,297
However, as the only child,

104
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:43,010
I am the only one who has the right
to make decisions regarding her condition.

105
00:05:45,179 --> 00:05:47,639
I have more right than you, Uncle Teddy.

106
00:05:50,142 --> 00:05:52,436
I can even ban you from coming here.

107
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:55,647
Am I right, attorney?

108
00:05:58,650 --> 00:06:00,152
I majored in Political Science.

109
00:06:00,986 --> 00:06:03,530
Pre-law. I'm educated.

110
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,951
However, I am not an Aragon.

111
00:06:08,952 --> 00:06:09,787
I am a Dela Cruz.

112
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:13,582
I won't involve myself in your mess.

113
00:06:13,999 --> 00:06:17,336
But don't walk all over me
because we all know

114
00:06:17,419 --> 00:06:20,255
I'm worth more than all of you.

115
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:21,673
That's it.

116
00:06:22,674 --> 00:06:25,677
I am right. You're after the inheritance.

117
00:06:25,761 --> 00:06:27,471
What kind of daughter are you?

118
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:34,603
Before you ask me
what kind of daughter I am,

119
00:06:34,686 --> 00:06:37,314
why don't you ask her
what kind of mother she is?

120
00:06:43,487 --> 00:06:46,281
-Wait, wait, wait. Wait.
-Why? Why?

121
00:06:46,365 --> 00:06:47,407
My feet hurt.

122
00:06:49,076 --> 00:06:51,120
I really thought
they were going to hurt us, Dad!

123
00:06:51,203 --> 00:06:53,956
That might be the case
if we hadn't escaped!

124
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:55,582
Call Patricia.

125
00:06:55,666 --> 00:06:57,751
Who knows what'll happen
if she comes home?

126
00:06:57,835 --> 00:07:01,755
I've been trying to call her,
but she's not picking up!

127
00:07:02,256 --> 00:07:03,215
Call her again!

128
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:04,925
Dad, where are we going to live?

129
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:07,553
Mom! Dad! Isn't this Patricia?

130
00:07:10,180 --> 00:07:11,765
What is she doing there?

131
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:16,687
Jena, are you sure
this is the hospital Patricia went to?

132
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:18,689
Yes, I'm sure this is that hospital!

133
00:07:18,772 --> 00:07:21,316
Oh? Aren't those reporters?

134
00:07:21,400 --> 00:07:22,234
I'm sorry.

135
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:24,903
Is she still here?

136
00:07:24,987 --> 00:07:28,407
Your sister's phone is still turned off.

137
00:07:28,991 --> 00:07:30,784
We should split into groups,

138
00:07:31,201 --> 00:07:33,412
-so we can find her quickly.
-All right, all right.

139
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:35,789
-I'll head in now.
-All right, sure. Sure.

140
00:07:35,873 --> 00:07:39,126
We'll leave you two here.
Keep a close eye on our stuff.

141
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:41,795
-If something gets lost…
-Yes, Mom.

142
00:07:41,879 --> 00:07:44,840
Bring it to the side. It's embarrassing!

143
00:07:48,135 --> 00:07:50,179
You know what I think?

144
00:07:50,262 --> 00:07:52,347
I think Diana Aragon's
in critical condition.

145
00:07:52,848 --> 00:07:56,685
I mean, it's been hours, right?
And there's still nothing.

146
00:07:56,768 --> 00:08:00,063
They don't even give updates
if she's still doing fine.

147
00:08:00,147 --> 00:08:02,900
Rumors say her daughter showed up.

148
00:08:02,983 --> 00:08:06,862
That's the story I want to know.
But she's lucky, isn't she?

149
00:08:06,945 --> 00:08:08,822
She's the only child.

150
00:08:08,906 --> 00:08:11,241
In other words,
she will inherit everything.

151
00:08:42,481 --> 00:08:43,690
Dad.

152
00:08:45,776 --> 00:08:47,986
Why didn't you tell me
where you were going?

153
00:08:48,946 --> 00:08:51,406
You're not even picking up our calls!

154
00:08:51,490 --> 00:08:54,368
If we hadn't seen you on the news,
we wouldn't have known where you are!

155
00:08:54,785 --> 00:08:56,787
My phone died. I'm sorry.

156
00:08:57,829 --> 00:08:59,373
What are you doing here?

157
00:09:00,832 --> 00:09:02,292
We were kicked out of the house.

158
00:09:02,376 --> 00:09:04,169
They even swarmed us!

159
00:09:04,253 --> 00:09:06,630
We can't go back there anymore.

160
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:08,924
Good thing I got your bag, Patricia.

161
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:11,551
At least I brought some of your clothes.

162
00:09:11,635 --> 00:09:12,970
-Ow. Ow. Ow.
-Thank you.

163
00:09:13,053 --> 00:09:18,433
-Dad? Are you all right?
-I'm fine. My legs just hurt.

164
00:09:18,517 --> 00:09:19,935
-Mom.
-Oh?

165
00:09:20,727 --> 00:09:22,646
I'm hungry, Mom.

166
00:09:23,313 --> 00:09:26,525
-I want that.
-Me too, Mom. I'm hungry.

167
00:09:26,608 --> 00:09:28,735
Mom, don't you have money?

168
00:09:28,819 --> 00:09:30,237
Wait, let me check.

169
00:09:31,655 --> 00:09:34,992
Oh, no, I don't think I have money left.

170
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,868
I-I'll handle it. I'll handle it.

171
00:09:37,327 --> 00:09:38,287
-Come on.
-Come on.

172
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:40,205
-Can you walk?
-I can.

173
00:09:41,832 --> 00:09:43,000
Yes, ma'am?

174
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,251
-What will you get?
-Uh, mister,

175
00:09:44,334 --> 00:09:46,962
how much is the Japanese siomai with rice?

176
00:09:47,045 --> 00:09:48,505
It's 50 pesos for one order, ma'am.

177
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:49,548
Fifty…

178
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,175
How many will you get?

179
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:55,137
-Four.
-Okay.

180
00:09:56,305 --> 00:09:58,056
-Here it is.
-Thank you.

181
00:09:59,308 --> 00:10:00,976
-Be careful.
-Thank you, Patricia!

182
00:10:01,059 --> 00:10:02,561
Thank you!

183
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,439
-How generous.
-Where's the spoon?

184
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:07,941
You even treated us siomai and rice.

185
00:10:08,025 --> 00:10:11,194
-Of course. Here, Dad.
-What about yours?

186
00:10:12,487 --> 00:10:13,488
I'm full.

187
00:10:14,114 --> 00:10:16,283
-Go eat.
-All right.

188
00:10:17,284 --> 00:10:18,285
Miss.

189
00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:20,329
Can I have some?

190
00:10:20,412 --> 00:10:22,205
-Hey, hey!
-Wait, wait.

191
00:10:22,289 --> 00:10:25,417
-Hey! Hey! Hey!
-Hey, wait! Hey!

192
00:10:26,418 --> 00:10:28,795
-Dad, let it go.
-Patricia…

193
00:10:30,005 --> 00:10:31,381
Are you okay? Did he hurt you?

194
00:10:31,965 --> 00:10:34,384
It's dangerous for us
to be on the streets.

195
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:38,430
-Anyone home?
-Patricia.

196
00:10:42,267 --> 00:10:43,602
Who are you?

197
00:10:44,061 --> 00:10:45,562
What are you doing here?

198
00:10:46,063 --> 00:10:48,482
She's Patricia, Diana's daughter.

199
00:10:48,565 --> 00:10:49,399
Daughter?

200
00:10:49,483 --> 00:10:51,401
But ma'am never mentioned anything.

201
00:10:51,943 --> 00:10:53,528
What's going on here?

202
00:10:54,446 --> 00:10:56,531
-Nanny Cora.
-Patricia?

203
00:10:57,366 --> 00:10:58,867
Patricia, is that you?

204
00:10:59,743 --> 00:11:00,660
Cora.

205
00:11:00,744 --> 00:11:03,830
Teach that man next time.

206
00:11:03,914 --> 00:11:05,457
He doesn't know who he's talking to.

207
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:08,210
He lacks manners.

208
00:11:09,753 --> 00:11:12,047
Uh, you'll have to excuse him.

209
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:15,175
Benjie wasn't here
when you were still here.

210
00:11:15,592 --> 00:11:19,554
Uh, Benjie, he's Martin…

211
00:11:19,638 --> 00:11:22,557
Ma'am Diana's ex-husband.

212
00:11:22,974 --> 00:11:29,064
She's Carlota, the daughter
of a former maid here.

213
00:11:29,523 --> 00:11:32,943
The Aragons funded her education,
and she worked in La Familia.

214
00:11:33,026 --> 00:11:35,695
She's Diana's close friend!

215
00:11:36,113 --> 00:11:37,614
Well, she used to be.

216
00:11:37,697 --> 00:11:42,577
Now, Martin and Carlota are married.

217
00:11:42,911 --> 00:11:46,331
You know them now, okay?

218
00:11:46,415 --> 00:11:48,583
Your introduction's pretty good.

219
00:11:49,084 --> 00:11:50,293
Oh! Hey.

220
00:11:51,002 --> 00:11:52,129
Why'd you come here?

221
00:11:52,754 --> 00:11:54,089
Uhm…

222
00:11:55,882 --> 00:11:58,593
Nanny Cora, can we stay here?

223
00:11:59,386 --> 00:12:01,179
We've got nowhere else to go.

224
00:12:01,888 --> 00:12:04,391
But just for now. We won't be long.

225
00:12:11,857 --> 00:12:13,316
Come in.

226
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:16,486
Wow! Are we going to live here now?

227
00:12:17,404 --> 00:12:18,864
Let's go.

228
00:12:44,306 --> 00:12:48,310
My gosh! This house is like a palace!

229
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:49,811
Palace?

230
00:12:51,688 --> 00:12:53,064
It's more like a mausoleum.

231
00:12:53,148 --> 00:12:56,485
You know, it's like
Diana completely forgot about you.

232
00:12:56,568 --> 00:12:58,361
Didn't you notice?

233
00:12:58,445 --> 00:13:00,697
You have no photos here. Not even one.

234
00:13:01,281 --> 00:13:03,408
Patricia, you should settle down for now.

235
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:07,787
I'll make you something to eat.

236
00:13:08,455 --> 00:13:09,414
Thank you.

237
00:13:47,244 --> 00:13:48,078
Mom.

238
00:13:50,247 --> 00:13:52,582
My gosh, Jena, you scared me.

239
00:13:52,666 --> 00:13:54,209
But they said breakfast is ready!

240
00:13:54,292 --> 00:13:56,002
What are you doing here, Mom?

241
00:13:57,170 --> 00:14:00,006
Nothing, I'm just checking something.

242
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:03,260
Wow!

243
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:07,681
Mom! Wow!

244
00:14:08,598 --> 00:14:11,226
Patricia's mom is so rich!

245
00:14:13,436 --> 00:14:15,021
-But Mom…
-Hm?

246
00:14:15,105 --> 00:14:17,357
Why didn't you tell us
Patricia's this rich?

247
00:14:17,691 --> 00:14:21,194
We live in poverty
when she can just ask for help.

248
00:14:21,278 --> 00:14:24,114
It's a long story, but the bottomline is…

249
00:14:24,406 --> 00:14:28,159
-that woman's a jerk.
-Oh! Wow, a jerk, really?

250
00:14:28,243 --> 00:14:31,496
Tell me. Have you ever thought
of leaving me?

251
00:14:31,580 --> 00:14:33,248
-No!
-Exactly!

252
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:37,294
Imagine how bad of a mother she is

253
00:14:37,377 --> 00:14:40,171
that her own child abandoned her!

254
00:14:40,422 --> 00:14:44,217
You know, ever since Patricia left Diana,

255
00:14:44,301 --> 00:14:49,639
not once did she ever
receive help from Diana.

256
00:14:49,723 --> 00:14:52,225
Patricia's been through a lot.

257
00:14:52,642 --> 00:14:55,395
We're still better because, at least…

258
00:14:55,812 --> 00:14:57,355
you love me, right?

259
00:14:57,439 --> 00:14:59,107
-You love me so much!
-Of course, Mom!

260
00:15:04,112 --> 00:15:08,450
Wow! Mom! Ahh! Mom, oh, my gosh!

261
00:15:09,451 --> 00:15:11,119
I only see this in celebrities' vlogs!

262
00:15:11,202 --> 00:15:13,747
-Yes.
-T-These bags?

263
00:15:13,830 --> 00:15:15,415
These cost millions!

264
00:15:15,874 --> 00:15:18,418
I think this suits me. I really think so.

265
00:15:19,377 --> 00:15:20,587
Wow!

266
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:22,339
Jena. Jena!

267
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:27,385
We now have a solution to our problems.

268
00:16:13,515 --> 00:16:15,975
Where's the dress I bought for you?

269
00:16:16,059 --> 00:16:17,686
Why are you wearing this?

270
00:16:18,353 --> 00:16:20,021
It was itchy.

271
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:22,399
So this is why you keep failing.

272
00:16:22,482 --> 00:16:24,484
All you do is watch TV.

273
00:16:35,078 --> 00:16:36,204
Patricia.

274
00:16:38,498 --> 00:16:39,541
My room's locked?

275
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:42,335
Your mom doesn't want it opened.

276
00:16:43,586 --> 00:16:45,296
She probably uses it for storage.

277
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:47,590
-Patricia.
-It's fine.

278
00:16:48,174 --> 00:16:49,467
I get it.

279
00:16:49,884 --> 00:16:52,846
-I'm nothing to her.
-But you showed up.

280
00:16:53,763 --> 00:16:54,848
You still visited her.

281
00:16:55,265 --> 00:16:58,685
That means you still worry
about her, right?

282
00:16:59,728 --> 00:17:02,897
I just checked to see
if I could get my inheritance.

283
00:17:05,942 --> 00:17:08,528
That's what Uncle Teddy's accusing me of.

284
00:17:10,864 --> 00:17:12,157
I know that's not true.

285
00:17:12,741 --> 00:17:16,828
I believe your mother
still has a place in your heart.

286
00:17:18,413 --> 00:17:23,168
I will never tire of praying
that you two will reconcile.

287
00:17:26,004 --> 00:17:28,590
Your vitals look good and stable now.

288
00:17:28,673 --> 00:17:32,260
There is no major neurological
damage or paralysis.

289
00:17:32,343 --> 00:17:35,638
Can I be discharged now?
I need to get back to work.

290
00:17:35,722 --> 00:17:37,766
Your body is still weak.

291
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:40,769
And as hospital protocol,
you have to be in a wheelchair

292
00:17:40,852 --> 00:17:42,729
when you move around for one to two days.

293
00:17:43,396 --> 00:17:45,648
You just suffered a heart attack.

294
00:17:45,732 --> 00:17:47,484
We're not taking any chances.

295
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:49,402
I'll be back for the other test results.

296
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:51,863
Thanks, Doc.

297
00:17:54,908 --> 00:17:56,326
Updates.

298
00:17:59,788 --> 00:18:01,706
Due to the poisoning issue,

299
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:04,209
our stock price has dropped significantly.

300
00:18:05,210 --> 00:18:08,421
Some supermarkets
also pulled out our products,

301
00:18:08,505 --> 00:18:10,632
which has led to a decline in sales.

302
00:18:10,715 --> 00:18:14,677
And the news coming out
aren't good either, Ms. D.

303
00:18:14,761 --> 00:18:16,346
The victims?

304
00:18:16,763 --> 00:18:18,556
We've paid for their hospitalization.

305
00:18:18,932 --> 00:18:22,185
Some of them were easy to pacify
and talk to.

306
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,813
We're still talking to the rest of them.

307
00:18:24,896 --> 00:18:27,941
Increase the financial help
to the victims.

308
00:18:28,733 --> 00:18:30,151
This needs to be fixed now.

309
00:18:30,568 --> 00:18:32,237
-Okay, ma'am.
-So…

310
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:34,906
Who's been in charge since I've been gone?

311
00:18:35,782 --> 00:18:38,368
Sir Teddy was appointed as interim CEO.

312
00:18:39,953 --> 00:18:44,082
Well, I'm awake now.
There's no need for that.

313
00:18:44,165 --> 00:18:45,542
Anything else?

314
00:18:46,334 --> 00:18:48,920
-Someone came to visit you.
-Who?

315
00:18:49,546 --> 00:18:52,173
-The Grim Reaper?
-It's Patricia.

316
00:18:57,887 --> 00:19:00,014
-Where is she?
-She left already.

317
00:19:02,475 --> 00:19:05,103
It seems Patricia's life hasn't been easy.

318
00:19:05,186 --> 00:19:08,189
She usually appears as a talent
in TV shows and movies.

319
00:19:08,273 --> 00:19:11,109
On the side, she sells whatever she could.

320
00:19:11,442 --> 00:19:13,278
Her father currently does not have a job.

321
00:19:13,361 --> 00:19:16,906
Her stepmother earns a small wage
in her job at the city hall,

322
00:19:17,323 --> 00:19:20,702
which is why Patricia is the breadwinner.

323
00:19:21,244 --> 00:19:23,872
She pays for everything,
even her sisters' education.

324
00:19:31,588 --> 00:19:34,465
-It's good that you've arrived.
-Good to see you're awake.

325
00:19:34,549 --> 00:19:36,467
And you don't have to worry about anything

326
00:19:36,551 --> 00:19:38,970
'cause I took care of everything
when you were sick.

327
00:19:39,345 --> 00:19:41,723
What have you done about the poisoning?

328
00:19:42,891 --> 00:19:47,186
Well, obviously, the crisis had
an impact on our brand.

329
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:48,771
Obviously.

330
00:19:48,855 --> 00:19:52,442
Have you released
a public statement about that?

331
00:19:52,525 --> 00:19:54,986
I mean, you're the head
of marketing, after all.

332
00:19:55,069 --> 00:19:56,779
I'm glad you asked, uh…

333
00:19:57,155 --> 00:19:59,741
We did. La Familia Corporation
official statement…

334
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:01,701
"La Familia Corporation
is aware of reports

335
00:20:01,784 --> 00:20:03,828
after consuming Cala Soda products…"

336
00:20:03,912 --> 00:20:05,163
Teddy. Teddy.

337
00:20:05,455 --> 00:20:08,791
So many people are hospitalized
because of that.

338
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:12,420
But all you're going to say
is you're "aware of reports"?

339
00:20:12,837 --> 00:20:15,048
How about, "We're deeply concerned,"

340
00:20:15,131 --> 00:20:19,093
or "We sincerely apologize
to the victims and their families"?

341
00:20:19,177 --> 00:20:21,971
-My gosh!
-You're right. We will revise.

342
00:20:22,055 --> 00:20:24,474
You should have thought about that, right?

343
00:20:27,602 --> 00:20:30,647
Did you see Patricia?
Did you kick her out?

344
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:34,067
She showed up after so many years, Diana.

345
00:20:34,442 --> 00:20:37,111
She thought you were dying,
and she'd get the inheritance.

346
00:20:38,071 --> 00:20:39,072
Well…

347
00:20:39,906 --> 00:20:45,036
I'm awake, alert, and alive,
but I'm not very enthusiastic.

348
00:20:45,495 --> 00:20:47,664
You know what I hate most?

349
00:20:47,914 --> 00:20:50,541
It's when someone decides for me.

350
00:20:50,917 --> 00:20:55,922
I'm the only one who can say
who's allowed and not allowed to visit me.

351
00:20:58,466 --> 00:20:59,300
Ms. D…

352
00:21:00,468 --> 00:21:02,845
-What's that now?
-You have to see this.

353
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:05,848
I have a surprise for you

354
00:21:05,932 --> 00:21:08,685
because this is a once
in a lifetime moment!

355
00:21:08,977 --> 00:21:11,396
These came from Italy!

356
00:21:11,479 --> 00:21:17,944
The very first item I'll sell
is this red Dior!

357
00:21:18,027 --> 00:21:19,779
It even smells like Italy!

358
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:24,575
But because I love you so, so much,

359
00:21:24,659 --> 00:21:27,578
I'll sell this for only 20,000 pesos!

360
00:21:27,662 --> 00:21:30,331
Item code is 001!

361
00:21:30,415 --> 00:21:32,083
Just for 20,000 pesos--

362
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:43,803
Patricia, what are you doing?

363
00:21:43,886 --> 00:21:48,182
-I'll fix that myself.
-No, it's fine. I can manage.

364
00:21:48,266 --> 00:21:50,393
I'm really the one
who should be doing this.

365
00:21:50,893 --> 00:21:53,062
I'm sorry we're being a bother.

366
00:21:53,396 --> 00:21:56,107
But I used to do that for you.

367
00:21:56,482 --> 00:21:58,234
Just think of what your mother would say.

368
00:21:58,484 --> 00:22:01,279
Nanny Cora, I spent more time
with you when I was a child

369
00:22:01,362 --> 00:22:02,488
than with my mother.

370
00:22:02,572 --> 00:22:06,951
But let me take care of you now.

371
00:22:07,326 --> 00:22:11,748
You know, in all honesty,
I've missed you so much.

372
00:22:11,831 --> 00:22:14,542
Don't be too attached, okay?

373
00:22:14,625 --> 00:22:16,586
I won't be here for long.

374
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:20,423
Besides, a lot of things
in my life have changed.

375
00:22:41,986 --> 00:22:43,029
Diana?

376
00:23:15,603 --> 00:23:16,896
Ms. D…

377
00:23:19,649 --> 00:23:21,234
Watch your step.

378
00:23:34,580 --> 00:23:35,748
Patricia.

379
00:23:36,999 --> 00:23:38,751
So, you've been discharged.

380
00:23:40,294 --> 00:23:42,338
How are you?

381
00:23:45,133 --> 00:23:46,134
Diana?!

382
00:23:49,554 --> 00:23:50,429
Oh.

383
00:23:51,097 --> 00:23:53,057
You look like you've just seen a ghost.

384
00:23:53,516 --> 00:23:54,934
I'm still alive, Carlota.

385
00:23:55,393 --> 00:23:57,103
And you still haven't changed.

386
00:23:57,728 --> 00:24:01,065
You're still digging through my trash.

387
00:24:06,779 --> 00:24:09,407
Couldn't you wait
before you celebrate my death?

388
00:24:09,991 --> 00:24:12,493
And did you really need
to do it in my house?

389
00:24:13,578 --> 00:24:17,039
It wasn't Dad and Mom
who decided to come here.

390
00:24:17,707 --> 00:24:18,666
It was me.

391
00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:24,505
Is this how you raised our child, Martin?

392
00:24:25,715 --> 00:24:27,758
A defender of wrongdoings.

393
00:24:28,384 --> 00:24:30,261
An enabler of theft.

394
00:24:31,262 --> 00:24:32,805
W-wait a minute.

395
00:24:33,389 --> 00:24:35,099
We're not stealing anything from you.

396
00:24:35,183 --> 00:24:37,185
She's trying to sell my stuff.

397
00:24:37,268 --> 00:24:38,561
What are you talking about?

398
00:24:41,939 --> 00:24:42,773
Mom!

399
00:24:43,691 --> 00:24:46,569
I didn't know she'd wake up.

400
00:24:46,652 --> 00:24:49,197
Besides, we're strapped for cash.

401
00:24:49,280 --> 00:24:51,199
You're such a leech!

402
00:24:51,282 --> 00:24:53,784
Ms. D, take it easy.
We'll take care of this.

403
00:24:53,868 --> 00:24:55,620
Benjie, security, please.

404
00:24:55,703 --> 00:24:56,704
-Hurry!
-Ah?

405
00:24:56,787 --> 00:24:58,789
W-wait a minute! Wait a minute!

406
00:24:58,873 --> 00:25:00,291
I'll give it back.

407
00:25:00,708 --> 00:25:02,585
Now, shove it down your lungs!

408
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:04,462
-Take it to your grave!
-That's enough.

409
00:25:04,545 --> 00:25:06,339
Who do you think you are?

410
00:25:06,422 --> 00:25:10,259
You're not even a good wife,
much less a good mother!

411
00:25:10,343 --> 00:25:11,844
-Mom, stop it.
-What are you going to do?

412
00:25:11,928 --> 00:25:13,846
You're no better than us, Diana.

413
00:25:13,930 --> 00:25:16,182
Sure, you're surrounded
by all these nice things,

414
00:25:16,265 --> 00:25:19,185
but we all know that you're alone.

415
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:22,021
You're all alone now
because no one can stand you!

416
00:25:22,104 --> 00:25:23,814
-Please, stop it.
-Right?

417
00:25:23,898 --> 00:25:25,316
-Come at me!
-Security, get them out please.

418
00:25:25,399 --> 00:25:26,609
Ma'am…

419
00:25:26,692 --> 00:25:28,527
No, I'm not leaving.

420
00:25:28,945 --> 00:25:30,696
-I'm not leaving!
-Mom!

421
00:25:30,780 --> 00:25:32,531
-I said, I'm not leaving!
-Mom, stop!

422
00:25:32,615 --> 00:25:33,658
That's enough.

423
00:25:33,741 --> 00:25:35,451
Let my mother go!

424
00:25:35,534 --> 00:25:38,663
-Mom, that's enough!
-Come with us!

425
00:25:38,746 --> 00:25:39,830
-Stop it!
-Dad!

426
00:25:41,958 --> 00:25:42,959
That's enough!

427
00:25:43,042 --> 00:25:44,669
Enough!

428
00:25:44,752 --> 00:25:46,128
Come on, let's get you up.

429
00:25:48,297 --> 00:25:50,591
You don't need to drag us out.

430
00:25:50,675 --> 00:25:52,718
I wouldn't even come here

431
00:25:52,802 --> 00:25:55,179
if I had somewhere else to go!

432
00:25:56,973 --> 00:25:59,475
I just thought you've changed.

433
00:26:00,851 --> 00:26:02,103
But I thought wrong.

434
00:26:03,771 --> 00:26:06,524
But that's on me. I should've known.

435
00:26:07,650 --> 00:26:10,361
Like when I asked for your help when…

436
00:26:10,903 --> 00:26:12,863
when I needed a mother,

437
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:16,284
you just let Dad get injured!

438
00:26:24,083 --> 00:26:26,127
Do you really think

439
00:26:27,461 --> 00:26:29,505
I'm a bad person?

440
00:26:30,965 --> 00:26:33,467
Well, that's what you're showing me.

441
00:26:34,635 --> 00:26:36,178
When Dad got into an accident,

442
00:26:38,848 --> 00:26:41,267
Mommy Carlota was there for us.

443
00:26:41,851 --> 00:26:44,729
So, you're defending a thief?

444
00:26:47,023 --> 00:26:48,149
All right.

445
00:26:50,234 --> 00:26:51,444
Call the cops.

446
00:26:52,653 --> 00:26:53,946
But all I want…

447
00:26:56,449 --> 00:26:58,242
is that you put me in jail instead.

448
00:27:03,581 --> 00:27:05,249
Not my mother.

449
00:27:06,083 --> 00:27:09,295
I want you to never touch my family again.

450
00:27:12,548 --> 00:27:13,966
You two.

451
00:27:15,801 --> 00:27:17,386
You got what you wanted.

452
00:27:19,013 --> 00:27:21,474
For the love of God, leave.

453
00:27:23,517 --> 00:27:25,061
Please, leave.

454
00:27:44,830 --> 00:27:46,999
Ms. D, take it easy.

455
00:27:48,125 --> 00:27:49,627
Should I still call the police?

456
00:27:49,710 --> 00:27:50,878
No.

457
00:28:06,560 --> 00:28:08,229
Patricia left it behind.

458
00:28:09,438 --> 00:28:12,316
Why did you let them all in?

459
00:28:13,109 --> 00:28:15,152
Because they needed help.

460
00:28:16,278 --> 00:28:17,947
Diana,

461
00:28:18,030 --> 00:28:19,990
Patricia is still your daughter.

462
00:28:24,745 --> 00:28:26,747
You think she still sees me as her mom?

463
00:28:30,751 --> 00:28:34,380
How long are you going to let this on?

464
00:28:35,631 --> 00:28:37,967
If you didn't have problems
in La Familia before,

465
00:28:38,050 --> 00:28:41,887
it wouldn't have ended up this way.

466
00:28:48,602 --> 00:28:50,521
You're always away!

467
00:28:57,778 --> 00:28:59,363
Not just that, Sir Lucio.

468
00:28:59,780 --> 00:29:02,074
There are missing funds.

469
00:29:02,158 --> 00:29:05,494
It's possible that there's
a conspiracy in the company.

470
00:29:05,578 --> 00:29:06,871
WHERE ARE YOU? PATRICIA'S LOOKING FOR YOU.

471
00:29:06,954 --> 00:29:08,289
PATRICIA'S PERFORMING NEXT.

472
00:29:08,372 --> 00:29:09,623
CAN YOU MAKE IT?
THE PROGRAM'S ALMOST OVER.

473
00:29:10,166 --> 00:29:13,502
Diana, we have urgent business here.

474
00:29:13,586 --> 00:29:14,753
Uh…

475
00:29:15,337 --> 00:29:18,591
I'm sorry, Dad.
Patricia has a school event today.

476
00:29:18,674 --> 00:29:20,509
We're facing a crisis in the company.

477
00:29:20,593 --> 00:29:23,095
We're losing millions of pesos.

478
00:29:23,179 --> 00:29:24,305
And you're worried about that?

479
00:29:24,930 --> 00:29:26,140
Why?

480
00:29:26,223 --> 00:29:28,976
Will that be Patricia's
last school performance?

481
00:29:29,768 --> 00:29:32,938
Will she die if you don't come?

482
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:39,612
I promised her, Dad.

483
00:29:40,821 --> 00:29:43,866
People's jobs depend on us.

484
00:29:44,366 --> 00:29:46,827
And you're risking all that

485
00:29:46,911 --> 00:29:49,830
just to go to a school program?

486
00:29:50,372 --> 00:29:52,458
Well then, if you want, leave!

487
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:55,503
And make sure to bring all of your stuff

488
00:29:55,586 --> 00:29:57,546
because you're not
coming back here anymore.

489
00:30:00,591 --> 00:30:03,552
What else do you want me to do?

490
00:30:04,929 --> 00:30:08,557
Don't you have
any other necklace that isn't tacky?

491
00:30:09,058 --> 00:30:11,977
Dad, what more do you want from me?

492
00:30:12,603 --> 00:30:15,272
When you asked me to choose
between you and Martin,

493
00:30:15,356 --> 00:30:19,735
I chose Martin because
we were building a family.

494
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:24,698
But you asked me to come back
because you don't trust Teddy.

495
00:30:24,782 --> 00:30:27,117
So, that's how you see it?

496
00:30:27,868 --> 00:30:30,704
You don't see it as you, making a mistake

497
00:30:30,788 --> 00:30:32,706
and I, forgiving you and letting you back?

498
00:30:33,290 --> 00:30:35,209
Is loving a mistake?

499
00:30:36,418 --> 00:30:39,046
Is choosing my family a mistake?

500
00:30:40,005 --> 00:30:42,758
This is not just because of the company.

501
00:30:43,968 --> 00:30:47,805
It's because you deserve
so much more better.

502
00:30:48,138 --> 00:30:51,141
Do you think you'll be happy

503
00:30:51,225 --> 00:30:53,936
and content with life as a housewife?

504
00:30:54,353 --> 00:30:56,897
You're just wasting
your skills and intellect

505
00:30:56,981 --> 00:30:59,275
on a man that isn't even on your level.

506
00:30:59,858 --> 00:31:02,069
My god, Diana!

507
00:31:02,152 --> 00:31:02,987
Admit it.

508
00:31:03,070 --> 00:31:05,447
If that man didn't get you pregnant,

509
00:31:05,531 --> 00:31:07,241
you wouldn't even marry him.

510
00:31:07,866 --> 00:31:09,326
I'm telling the truth!

511
00:31:09,410 --> 00:31:10,578
You are thieves!

512
00:31:10,661 --> 00:31:15,332
How can I trust you with the company
if you keep messing up like this?

513
00:31:15,416 --> 00:31:16,458
Huh?

514
00:31:17,209 --> 00:31:20,838
I let you organize an event,
and what happened?

515
00:31:20,921 --> 00:31:22,214
It was a failure!

516
00:31:23,048 --> 00:31:24,925
Can't you make a good decision for once?

517
00:31:25,259 --> 00:31:27,720
First, that husband of yours.

518
00:31:28,095 --> 00:31:31,265
You married a born loser!

519
00:31:31,348 --> 00:31:33,309
Just accept it, Dad.

520
00:31:33,392 --> 00:31:35,561
Martin is my husband and we have a child.

521
00:31:36,604 --> 00:31:39,690
Just let me know if you can't do it,

522
00:31:39,773 --> 00:31:42,776
and let's burn La Familia to the ground!

523
00:31:42,860 --> 00:31:45,946
Instead of marrying an honorable man,

524
00:31:46,030 --> 00:31:50,117
you chose a lowly employee of La Familia.

525
00:31:50,784 --> 00:31:53,203
You chose an idiot!

526
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:57,041
My Dad is not an idiot!

527
00:31:57,416 --> 00:31:59,209
-Patricia.
-I can call your father

528
00:31:59,293 --> 00:32:00,419
whatever I want.

529
00:32:00,794 --> 00:32:02,588
You're an Aragon.

530
00:32:02,963 --> 00:32:05,883
Learn to act like one.

531
00:32:05,966 --> 00:32:08,552
Patricia, please wait outside.

532
00:32:09,803 --> 00:32:11,013
Patricia.

533
00:32:17,645 --> 00:32:19,229
Did you see that?

534
00:32:19,772 --> 00:32:22,399
Your daughter already learned
how to talk back to me!

535
00:32:23,567 --> 00:32:26,195
She's just defending her father.

536
00:32:26,820 --> 00:32:29,948
She's not your employee or a board member.

537
00:32:30,866 --> 00:32:34,453
I won't let you treat her
the way you treat me.

538
00:32:35,537 --> 00:32:36,664
Dad.

539
00:32:37,247 --> 00:32:39,792
Whatever disappointment you have in me,

540
00:32:39,875 --> 00:32:41,794
don't pass it on to my daughter.

541
00:32:42,711 --> 00:32:44,922
I will fix what happened tonight.

542
00:32:45,422 --> 00:32:49,718
But when it comes to my child,
I call the shots, Dad.

543
00:32:50,260 --> 00:32:53,639
I may not be the ideal father to you.

544
00:32:54,515 --> 00:32:56,016
But don't ever forget.

545
00:32:56,100 --> 00:32:58,394
Every time I was hard on you,

546
00:32:58,811 --> 00:33:02,648
it's because I know
you have what it takes.

547
00:33:03,482 --> 00:33:05,776
It's a cruel world out there!

548
00:33:05,859 --> 00:33:08,696
I treat you like this to strengthen you.

549
00:33:10,114 --> 00:33:11,031
Diana.

550
00:33:12,616 --> 00:33:15,744
You are meant to lead La Familia.

551
00:33:16,328 --> 00:33:17,996
This is our legacy.

552
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:20,082
Promise me.

553
00:33:20,582 --> 00:33:22,835
Promise me, you will stay strong.

554
00:33:23,961 --> 00:33:28,882
Promise me you won't let La Familia down.

555
00:33:38,183 --> 00:33:39,518
Dad!

556
00:33:48,485 --> 00:33:49,403
Ma'am.

557
00:33:49,862 --> 00:33:51,238
Give me an update.

558
00:33:51,697 --> 00:33:54,992
Ten people died, all factory employees.

559
00:33:55,075 --> 00:33:56,326
Two were injured.

560
00:33:56,827 --> 00:33:58,620
Sir Lucio and…

561
00:33:58,704 --> 00:34:00,539
Cecilia Pineda.

562
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:02,458
We're just waiting for her to wake up.

563
00:34:02,541 --> 00:34:04,001
We've also informed her family.

564
00:34:04,084 --> 00:34:06,712
What was Dad doing in the factory?

565
00:34:07,129 --> 00:34:10,924
The clients are breathing down our necks
ever since production stopped.

566
00:34:11,383 --> 00:34:13,010
The banks are following up as well.

567
00:34:13,093 --> 00:34:14,511
What did our insurance say?

568
00:34:14,595 --> 00:34:16,555
We have to rebuild as soon as possible.

569
00:34:17,097 --> 00:34:20,350
I'm waiting for the final report
from the fire protection

570
00:34:20,434 --> 00:34:24,062
to confirm if it was
a case of arson or not.

571
00:34:26,607 --> 00:34:28,066
Ma'am.

572
00:34:43,165 --> 00:34:44,708
Why do you have this?

573
00:34:45,542 --> 00:34:46,710
Did you light it inside the factory?

574
00:34:46,794 --> 00:34:48,879
Patricia, tell me! What did you do?

575
00:34:50,589 --> 00:34:52,466
Are you sure?

576
00:34:52,549 --> 00:34:53,926
Did he really say that?

577
00:34:54,468 --> 00:34:55,719
Yes, sir.

578
00:34:55,803 --> 00:34:58,305
I heard Grandpa say it.

579
00:34:58,847 --> 00:35:01,433
"Let's burn La Familia to the ground."

580
00:35:01,850 --> 00:35:04,102
Excuse me? Who are you?

581
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:06,104
We're police investigators, ma'am.

582
00:35:06,772 --> 00:35:09,691
We just have some follow-up
questions about the fire.

583
00:35:09,775 --> 00:35:13,445
And I am the insurance investigator
who handles the property claim.

584
00:35:14,321 --> 00:35:16,865
Why are you interrogating my daughter?

585
00:35:16,949 --> 00:35:20,285
We need to look at every angle.

586
00:35:20,369 --> 00:35:22,579
And your daughter
happened to be in the scene.

587
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:24,790
But you don't have permission.

588
00:35:24,873 --> 00:35:26,667
She's just a child.

589
00:35:27,334 --> 00:35:29,127
I let them in, Diana.

590
00:35:29,211 --> 00:35:30,420
They were just asking questions.

591
00:35:30,504 --> 00:35:32,381
And I'm here to supervise.

592
00:35:39,930 --> 00:35:42,933
Patricia, why did you say that?

593
00:35:43,392 --> 00:35:44,893
Why did you say that?

594
00:35:44,977 --> 00:35:47,604
I just said what I heard Grandpa say.

595
00:35:51,400 --> 00:35:53,777
You ruined everything!

596
00:35:58,365 --> 00:36:00,742
Go home. I'll call the driver.

597
00:36:01,451 --> 00:36:03,787
-But, Mom…
-Patricia!

598
00:36:03,871 --> 00:36:05,747
For once, would you listen to me?

599
00:36:06,456 --> 00:36:11,628
You don't understand!
You have no idea what a huge mess this is!

600
00:36:12,880 --> 00:36:14,172
Go home!

601
00:36:14,548 --> 00:36:16,133
Go home!

602
00:36:22,306 --> 00:36:23,724
Code blue!

603
00:36:25,350 --> 00:36:27,561
-Excuse me.
-Dad…

604
00:36:28,061 --> 00:36:31,273
Ma'am, I'm sorry.
You need to stay out here.

605
00:36:31,982 --> 00:36:34,443
No heartbeat. Start compression.

606
00:36:51,168 --> 00:36:54,338
Time of death: 5:17 p.m.

607
00:36:55,797 --> 00:36:57,299
Dad…

608
00:36:59,176 --> 00:37:00,594
Dad!

609
00:37:03,388 --> 00:37:05,599
No… No, Dad.

610
00:38:02,364 --> 00:38:03,448
Diana, stop it!

611
00:38:03,532 --> 00:38:05,409
-That's enough!
-Let me go, you bastard!

612
00:38:05,492 --> 00:38:07,619
-That's enough!
-You bastard!

613
00:38:08,954 --> 00:38:11,123
You traitor! And you!

614
00:38:11,456 --> 00:38:13,875
I thought you were my friend!

615
00:38:13,959 --> 00:38:15,627
I treated you as family!

616
00:38:15,711 --> 00:38:19,381
How could you do this to me?!

617
00:38:19,881 --> 00:38:22,092
-Diana, that's enough!
-You left him!

618
00:38:22,509 --> 00:38:24,094
I was the only one there to catch him.

619
00:38:24,177 --> 00:38:26,972
You can't always be the lucky one, Diana.

620
00:38:27,055 --> 00:38:29,182
You think you can always get
anything you want?

621
00:38:29,266 --> 00:38:31,476
Why? Because you're rich, huh?!

622
00:38:32,019 --> 00:38:32,894
Diana!

623
00:38:32,978 --> 00:38:34,938
Our marriage has been struggling
for a long time!

624
00:38:36,523 --> 00:38:38,900
We have a child.

625
00:38:39,484 --> 00:38:42,195
Did you even think about her, huh?!

626
00:38:42,279 --> 00:38:44,281
You didn't even think about her!

627
00:38:46,950 --> 00:38:50,370
You don't deserve me!

628
00:38:50,454 --> 00:38:51,663
No!

629
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:58,920
Do you want to be
with your mom or your dad?

630
00:38:59,004 --> 00:39:00,213
I want to be with Dad.

631
00:39:03,425 --> 00:39:04,509
Diana?

632
00:39:05,343 --> 00:39:08,638
Wait. What are you doing here?

633
00:39:08,722 --> 00:39:10,348
Our marriage has been annulled.
Don't make a scene.

634
00:39:10,599 --> 00:39:12,934
I separated with you,
but not with my daughter.

635
00:39:13,226 --> 00:39:15,103
If I lose my patience,
I'm going to send you to jail.

636
00:39:15,187 --> 00:39:16,188
Wait.

637
00:39:17,064 --> 00:39:19,024
Don't send Dad to jail!

638
00:39:21,068 --> 00:39:22,611
Patricia.

639
00:39:22,694 --> 00:39:24,154
Enough, okay?

640
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:25,655
You've already proven your point.

641
00:39:25,739 --> 00:39:26,865
Let's go home, dear.

642
00:39:26,948 --> 00:39:28,784
Are you going to make it hard for the kid?

643
00:39:33,914 --> 00:39:36,041
I let you meet her freely.

644
00:39:36,124 --> 00:39:38,752
That's why I agreed to visitation rights.

645
00:39:38,835 --> 00:39:40,796
Why do you have to take
my daughter away from me?

646
00:39:40,879 --> 00:39:42,589
Because she chose to be with me.

647
00:39:42,672 --> 00:39:45,175
What? Do you think I'm having fun at work?

648
00:39:45,258 --> 00:39:46,468
I'm doing this for her future.

649
00:39:46,551 --> 00:39:47,844
I'm doing this for your future.

650
00:39:47,928 --> 00:39:50,639
Future? If we go home,

651
00:39:50,722 --> 00:39:52,974
are you going to finally be a mother?

652
00:39:53,266 --> 00:39:55,018
Are you going to start loving me?

653
00:39:55,102 --> 00:39:58,355
Or will you still blame me
for what happened to Grandpa?

654
00:39:58,438 --> 00:40:00,482
You don't know what you're talking about.

655
00:40:00,857 --> 00:40:02,859
I don't want to go with you!

656
00:40:05,112 --> 00:40:09,950
Is the annulment settlement
not enough for you?

657
00:40:10,659 --> 00:40:13,495
I've given you everything you asked for,

658
00:40:13,578 --> 00:40:15,497
but that doesn't include my daughter.

659
00:40:16,081 --> 00:40:17,958
I am going to file for sole custody.

660
00:40:18,041 --> 00:40:19,167
Do it.

661
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:21,253
See you in court.

662
00:40:21,962 --> 00:40:22,796
Let's go.

663
00:40:28,426 --> 00:40:31,805
Martin poisoned Patricia's heart
a long time ago.

664
00:40:34,141 --> 00:40:38,436
I understand how you feel.

665
00:40:38,520 --> 00:40:41,231
I understand Patricia as well.

666
00:40:41,314 --> 00:40:45,026
I know you both have
unresolved issues with each other.

667
00:40:45,318 --> 00:40:49,489
Patricia was the one who decided
to cut me off from her life.

668
00:40:51,616 --> 00:40:54,494
When does motherhood end?

669
00:40:54,870 --> 00:40:56,705
I did fine on my own.

670
00:40:58,248 --> 00:41:00,292
If she doesn't need me anymore,

671
00:41:01,334 --> 00:41:02,836
then I won't need her either.

672
00:41:03,336 --> 00:41:04,462
But…

673
00:41:05,255 --> 00:41:06,506
are you happy?

674
00:41:07,674 --> 00:41:08,800
Happy?

675
00:41:10,594 --> 00:41:13,638
I took the entire La Familia
out of the ashes.

676
00:41:14,139 --> 00:41:15,390
And if Patricia thinks

677
00:41:15,473 --> 00:41:17,267
that makes me
the worst person in the world,

678
00:41:17,350 --> 00:41:19,019
there's nothing I can do about it.

679
00:41:19,728 --> 00:41:22,814
I can accept that she doesn't
care about me anymore.

680
00:41:26,443 --> 00:41:28,653
If you can only go back--

681
00:41:28,737 --> 00:41:32,866
We can't go back
to the way things were, Nanny Cora.

682
00:41:34,659 --> 00:41:36,536
But I believe…

683
00:41:38,246 --> 00:41:39,831
that there is a reason…

684
00:41:39,915 --> 00:41:41,708
why you two met again.

685
00:41:49,799 --> 00:41:50,675
There…

686
00:41:50,759 --> 00:41:52,761
I'm glad you picked up last night.

687
00:41:52,844 --> 00:41:54,638
I have no one else to call.

688
00:41:54,721 --> 00:41:55,931
Don't worry about it.

689
00:41:56,014 --> 00:41:58,099
I usually sleep late.

690
00:41:58,183 --> 00:41:59,142
-Bestie.
-Hmm?

691
00:41:59,226 --> 00:42:00,852
You can borrow and use this for now.

692
00:42:00,936 --> 00:42:02,604
Okay. Thank you.

693
00:42:02,687 --> 00:42:03,897
-This way. Careful.
-No problem.

694
00:42:03,980 --> 00:42:07,234
Thankfully, my aunt had
a place available for tenants.

695
00:42:07,317 --> 00:42:10,445
That means we can now go
to auditions together.

696
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:12,030
Mm. You're right.

697
00:42:12,113 --> 00:42:13,657
Oh, thank you.

698
00:42:13,740 --> 00:42:15,992
Did you receive a text?
They're looking for talents today.

699
00:42:16,076 --> 00:42:17,827
Yes. Do you want to go together?

700
00:42:17,911 --> 00:42:19,204
-I'll just go to the restroom.
-Mm.

701
00:42:19,287 --> 00:42:20,121
Okay.

702
00:42:20,830 --> 00:42:21,790
Patricia.

703
00:42:22,499 --> 00:42:24,084
Thank you.

704
00:42:24,501 --> 00:42:26,836
Because you're still thinking about us.

705
00:42:27,170 --> 00:42:28,755
Just remember…

706
00:42:28,838 --> 00:42:31,383
you're all my responsibility.

707
00:42:31,466 --> 00:42:32,842
I will never abandon you.

708
00:42:32,926 --> 00:42:34,678
Thank you, Patricia.

709
00:42:35,804 --> 00:42:37,389
Uh, Patricia.

710
00:42:37,472 --> 00:42:40,558
I think working as a talent
won't suffice now.

711
00:42:40,642 --> 00:42:44,980
Looks like you need to find a regular job.

712
00:42:45,438 --> 00:42:47,565
Our living cost is increasing.

713
00:42:47,649 --> 00:42:51,736
My salary can't cover all of it.

714
00:42:52,445 --> 00:42:53,363
Don't worry.

715
00:42:54,072 --> 00:42:56,449
Once I open a business and hit it big,

716
00:42:56,533 --> 00:42:57,993
you won't have to work.

717
00:43:00,328 --> 00:43:02,914
-Bestie, are you ready?
-Mm-hmm. Let's go.

718
00:43:02,998 --> 00:43:05,333
Wait. Let me walk you out.

719
00:43:05,417 --> 00:43:06,334
Okay.

720
00:43:06,418 --> 00:43:07,711
-Take care, okay?
-We will.

721
00:43:08,545 --> 00:43:09,713
-We'll go now.
-Stay safe.

722
00:43:09,796 --> 00:43:11,673
April, you take care of that.

723
00:43:14,175 --> 00:43:16,344
It's so annoying!

724
00:43:17,012 --> 00:43:17,846
We were already in a mansion.

725
00:43:17,929 --> 00:43:20,056
Why do we have to go back
to something like this? Gosh!

726
00:43:20,140 --> 00:43:23,268
You know, Jena, this is better
than having no house at all.

727
00:43:23,810 --> 00:43:27,480
I'm still mad about what
Patricia's mom did to us.

728
00:43:29,149 --> 00:43:30,567
It's really unfortunate.

729
00:43:30,650 --> 00:43:33,194
My pictures turned out great.
Only if I could post them.

730
00:43:35,030 --> 00:43:38,158
I get so annoyed
every time I see Ms. Diana's face here.

731
00:43:38,241 --> 00:43:40,577
See her face? What?

732
00:43:41,119 --> 00:43:42,329
Here, Mom.

733
00:43:42,412 --> 00:43:44,456
I was able to film what she did to us.

734
00:43:45,040 --> 00:43:46,124
Look.

735
00:43:53,381 --> 00:43:56,926
We've already reached
settlement with some of the victims.

736
00:43:57,010 --> 00:43:59,137
Others need a little more convincing,

737
00:43:59,220 --> 00:44:02,098
but I'm confident
that we'll overcome this.

738
00:44:02,682 --> 00:44:05,560
What I want is for us to move forward.

739
00:44:05,935 --> 00:44:08,355
I'm already setting
a meeting with Burger City

740
00:44:08,438 --> 00:44:09,689
to fix what happened.

741
00:44:09,773 --> 00:44:10,815
Excuse me. That's good,

742
00:44:10,899 --> 00:44:13,943
but it looks like we have
another PR nightmare.

743
00:44:16,029 --> 00:44:17,864
What are you talking about?

744
00:44:18,948 --> 00:44:20,742
Georgia just sent this to me.

745
00:44:21,326 --> 00:44:23,787
It's trending on social media,
and it's about you

746
00:44:24,371 --> 00:44:26,039
and Patricia's family.

747
00:44:27,665 --> 00:44:28,917
April, stop.

748
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:30,335
That's enough!

749
00:44:30,835 --> 00:44:33,004
-Guards, that's enough!
-Enough of this!

750
00:44:35,382 --> 00:44:36,925
You two.

751
00:44:38,551 --> 00:44:40,387
You got what you wanted.

752
00:44:41,596 --> 00:44:43,681
"Is that supposed to be the chairmom?

753
00:44:43,765 --> 00:44:45,975
-More like chairmonster."
-Enough.

754
00:44:46,309 --> 00:44:49,104
"That's why her daughter
refuses to see her…"

755
00:44:49,187 --> 00:44:50,772
-I said enough.
-"What…"

756
00:44:50,855 --> 00:44:52,315
I'm sorry. I'm just reading the comments.

757
00:44:52,399 --> 00:44:55,235
For decades, the image of La Familia

758
00:44:55,318 --> 00:44:56,945
is "always together with the family"

759
00:44:57,028 --> 00:44:59,447
and "the silent member of the family."

760
00:44:59,531 --> 00:45:01,032
This will affect the brand.

761
00:45:01,533 --> 00:45:03,660
Who's going to believe in our brand now?

762
00:45:04,119 --> 00:45:05,412
You know how people are.

763
00:45:05,495 --> 00:45:08,581
They don't like fighting
with your own flesh and blood.

764
00:45:08,665 --> 00:45:10,625
Our stocks are being monitored.

765
00:45:10,708 --> 00:45:12,752
If we don't control this right away--

766
00:45:12,836 --> 00:45:15,046
La Familia has been through worse.

767
00:45:15,130 --> 00:45:17,340
Much worse than just a stupid viral video.

768
00:45:18,258 --> 00:45:20,718
I suggest everyone remember that

769
00:45:20,802 --> 00:45:23,304
before you panic like amateurs.

770
00:45:23,388 --> 00:45:25,348
You know our bylaws, Diana.

771
00:45:25,432 --> 00:45:29,352
If the value of our shares drops by 30%,

772
00:45:29,436 --> 00:45:31,104
the poison pill clause will take effect.

773
00:45:31,187 --> 00:45:33,273
You're going to dilute my shares?

774
00:45:33,356 --> 00:45:35,483
There's already a talk, internally.

775
00:45:36,568 --> 00:45:40,029
It's about leadership stability.

776
00:45:40,113 --> 00:45:41,865
If this keeps happening…

777
00:45:41,948 --> 00:45:44,993
If public confidence keeps dropping,

778
00:45:45,076 --> 00:45:48,455
I think we may have
to change the leadership.

779
00:45:48,538 --> 00:45:49,664
Ah.

780
00:45:51,541 --> 00:45:53,918
So all of this boils down to that?

781
00:45:54,210 --> 00:45:58,047
One incident and you're already
discussing replacement.

782
00:45:58,131 --> 00:45:59,340
Let me be clear.

783
00:45:59,424 --> 00:46:02,635
La Familia will stabilize.

784
00:46:02,719 --> 00:46:04,888
The company will recover.

785
00:46:04,971 --> 00:46:06,306
And when that happens,

786
00:46:07,307 --> 00:46:11,853
I expect every single person
in this room, questioning me…

787
00:46:11,936 --> 00:46:14,564
and those who are quick to forget

788
00:46:15,190 --> 00:46:18,735
to remember that I…

789
00:46:18,818 --> 00:46:20,653
kept La Familia standing.

790
00:46:22,447 --> 00:46:24,699
Meeting adjourned.

791
00:46:31,206 --> 00:46:32,916
Ungrateful fools!

792
00:46:34,042 --> 00:46:35,627
Hey, are you okay?

793
00:46:36,085 --> 00:46:37,170
I'm fine.

794
00:46:39,422 --> 00:46:40,673
You know,

795
00:46:42,175 --> 00:46:44,427
I think you should hear them out.

796
00:46:46,888 --> 00:46:48,640
Hear them out?

797
00:46:49,474 --> 00:46:51,518
After everything I have done
for this company?

798
00:46:53,019 --> 00:46:54,938
Look, I'm not saying that you're wrong.

799
00:46:55,021 --> 00:46:56,564
But… but they're not totally wrong.

800
00:46:56,981 --> 00:46:58,024
I'm sorry, Teddy.

801
00:46:58,107 --> 00:47:00,401
But you're the last person
I'll ask for advice.

802
00:47:01,361 --> 00:47:03,655
You know, you and Dad…

803
00:47:05,448 --> 00:47:06,658
You're totally alike.

804
00:47:06,741 --> 00:47:09,619
Your world revolves around this company.

805
00:47:10,245 --> 00:47:12,413
You've sold your soul for this company.

806
00:47:12,956 --> 00:47:15,458
Are you conspiring with them, Teddy?

807
00:47:15,542 --> 00:47:17,085
What are you talking about?

808
00:47:17,544 --> 00:47:19,837
-I'm on your side. I'm your brother.
-Oh, cut the crap!

809
00:47:20,380 --> 00:47:23,091
I'm sorry that your dream
to replace me didn't come true.

810
00:47:23,174 --> 00:47:25,260
-Oh, come on, Diana.
-Isn't it true?

811
00:47:26,594 --> 00:47:28,429
You wanted to do that
since you went back home, right?

812
00:47:29,222 --> 00:47:31,724
After Dad died,

813
00:47:31,808 --> 00:47:32,934
you took your inheritance

814
00:47:33,017 --> 00:47:35,770
because you said you wanted
to start on your own.

815
00:47:35,853 --> 00:47:37,647
But what happened? You came back.

816
00:47:38,231 --> 00:47:40,066
Because you failed.

817
00:47:41,568 --> 00:47:44,612
I will never allow you
to do that to La Familia.

818
00:47:46,990 --> 00:47:49,033
I am La Familia.

819
00:47:50,243 --> 00:47:53,496
I will not let you ruin this company.

820
00:47:55,290 --> 00:47:57,166
But, Mom, that was wrong.

821
00:47:59,043 --> 00:48:01,421
I'm in the wrong again.

822
00:48:01,838 --> 00:48:03,381
Why are you…

823
00:48:03,464 --> 00:48:07,385
taking Diana's side?

824
00:48:10,054 --> 00:48:11,431
Oh, well…

825
00:48:11,848 --> 00:48:14,892
She's the one who gave birth to you.

826
00:48:15,310 --> 00:48:16,811
Who am I compared to her?

827
00:48:16,894 --> 00:48:18,563
I'm the one who raised you.

828
00:48:23,818 --> 00:48:26,029
I'm not taking her side.

829
00:48:27,572 --> 00:48:30,033
I'm just saying
that you did the wrong thing.

830
00:48:30,491 --> 00:48:32,493
Her giving birth to me
has nothing to do with this.

831
00:48:32,869 --> 00:48:34,912
You shouldn't have spread the video.

832
00:48:37,332 --> 00:48:39,083
People need to feel

833
00:48:39,167 --> 00:48:42,795
that La Familia is still the brand
that they grew up with.

834
00:48:43,796 --> 00:48:46,049
Let's go back to the emotional roots.

835
00:48:46,132 --> 00:48:47,842
Family values.

836
00:48:47,925 --> 00:48:49,093
Warmth.

837
00:48:49,177 --> 00:48:51,846
-Unity.
-No, no. Joey, stop.

838
00:48:51,929 --> 00:48:53,640
Diana, is there a problem?

839
00:48:53,723 --> 00:48:55,224
Yes, Joey.

840
00:48:55,767 --> 00:48:57,393
It's safe, predictable.

841
00:48:57,477 --> 00:49:00,730
It's like a Christmas
or Valentine's Day campaign.

842
00:49:00,813 --> 00:49:02,732
-Diana.
-It's same old, same old.

843
00:49:02,815 --> 00:49:05,485
I don't know anything!
You're accusing me of the wrong thing!

844
00:49:05,568 --> 00:49:07,028
You don't know anything?!

845
00:49:07,111 --> 00:49:08,863
Take this!

846
00:49:10,198 --> 00:49:11,115
Hold! Hold!

847
00:49:11,199 --> 00:49:13,701
Okay. Double, out. Bianca, go!

848
00:49:14,077 --> 00:49:15,036
Double, out!

849
00:49:17,038 --> 00:49:18,247
Ah, wait! Cut, cut!

850
00:49:18,873 --> 00:49:20,833
-Let's do it again.
-Again?

851
00:49:20,917 --> 00:49:23,378
So, Chairmom Diana,

852
00:49:23,461 --> 00:49:28,091
we plan to rebuild trust
through sincerity.

853
00:49:28,174 --> 00:49:29,384
As you can see…

854
00:49:29,967 --> 00:49:31,552
-Next!
-Action!

855
00:49:31,636 --> 00:49:34,180
I don't know anything!
You're accusing me of the wrong thing!

856
00:49:34,263 --> 00:49:35,932
You don't know anything?!

857
00:49:36,015 --> 00:49:37,934
Take this!

858
00:49:39,852 --> 00:49:43,356
Hold! Okay. Out, double! Bianca, go!

859
00:49:43,439 --> 00:49:46,359
I propose that we launch

860
00:49:46,442 --> 00:49:50,113
with a major apology campaign.

861
00:49:50,863 --> 00:49:52,073
Pathetic. Next!

862
00:49:52,156 --> 00:49:53,700
-Ah!
-Next!

863
00:49:56,119 --> 00:49:57,620
-Next!
-Damn you!

864
00:49:58,121 --> 00:50:00,832
You damn witch!

865
00:50:02,500 --> 00:50:05,253
Hold! Out! Double, out! Bianca, in!

866
00:50:06,212 --> 00:50:08,005
From your line, Bianca, okay?

867
00:50:08,089 --> 00:50:09,632
Stop!

868
00:50:10,258 --> 00:50:12,510
I didn't steal anything from you!

869
00:50:12,593 --> 00:50:15,471
He was in love with me first!

870
00:50:15,555 --> 00:50:19,142
Cut! Good take, actors!
Very good, very good.

871
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:23,020
This is so frustrating.

872
00:50:23,104 --> 00:50:24,355
I know, Ms. D.

873
00:50:24,439 --> 00:50:26,065
Look, we still have one last pitch.

874
00:50:26,149 --> 00:50:27,316
Well, send them in.

875
00:50:37,285 --> 00:50:38,828
And you are?

876
00:50:42,707 --> 00:50:43,750
Ricardo Salvador.

877
00:50:44,083 --> 00:50:46,711
PR consultant. Crisis Management Expert.

878
00:50:47,003 --> 00:50:51,174
I've worked with politicians,
celebrities, corporations.

879
00:50:51,257 --> 00:50:53,092
And Silver Graph Hall of Famer.

880
00:50:54,343 --> 00:50:55,219
What agency is he from?

881
00:50:56,512 --> 00:50:58,598
Ms. D, it doesn't seem
like he has an agency.

882
00:50:59,515 --> 00:51:00,391
I'm independent.

883
00:51:01,434 --> 00:51:03,102
I represent myself.

884
00:51:03,186 --> 00:51:05,438
So, what's your advertising campaign?

885
00:51:05,521 --> 00:51:07,690
That's your first mistake.

886
00:51:08,149 --> 00:51:09,442
Excuse me?

887
00:51:09,942 --> 00:51:12,779
You see it as an advertising issue.

888
00:51:13,654 --> 00:51:15,823
Your problem is an image crisis.

889
00:51:16,783 --> 00:51:18,785
Diana, your problem is…

890
00:51:19,952 --> 00:51:21,662
You're lying too much.

891
00:51:22,246 --> 00:51:24,999
For decades, you've shown
that a family is perfect

892
00:51:25,291 --> 00:51:27,335
as long as they have
Cala Soda on their table.

893
00:51:27,960 --> 00:51:30,254
You portray La Familia
as something perfect.

894
00:51:32,006 --> 00:51:35,259
That's why you called yourself
the chairmom.

895
00:51:37,720 --> 00:51:39,347
That's not real, Diana.

896
00:51:40,723 --> 00:51:42,225
You have to show the truth.

897
00:51:42,892 --> 00:51:44,519
A family can be messy.

898
00:51:44,602 --> 00:51:47,104
Sometimes they fight,
scream at each other,

899
00:51:47,188 --> 00:51:48,397
or hurt each other.

900
00:51:49,065 --> 00:51:50,650
But at the end of the day,

901
00:51:52,109 --> 00:51:53,319
they are still a family.

902
00:51:54,237 --> 00:51:56,155
What commercial do you have in mind?

903
00:51:56,739 --> 00:52:00,326
You don't need
another fake smiling campaign.

904
00:52:00,660 --> 00:52:02,203
What you need…

905
00:52:02,829 --> 00:52:05,289
is a tell-all sit-down interview.

906
00:52:05,748 --> 00:52:06,874
Interview?

907
00:52:08,793 --> 00:52:11,879
People think they know your story.

908
00:52:13,464 --> 00:52:14,799
So…

909
00:52:16,884 --> 00:52:18,261
Give them your own version

910
00:52:18,970 --> 00:52:20,638
before somebody else does.

911
00:52:20,721 --> 00:52:23,349
And you think that should fix everything?

912
00:52:23,432 --> 00:52:24,934
Of course not.

913
00:52:26,060 --> 00:52:27,937
But it changes the conversation.

914
00:52:30,439 --> 00:52:31,607
Diana.

915
00:52:32,692 --> 00:52:34,819
Right now, people see you as someone…

916
00:52:35,528 --> 00:52:36,571
untouchable.

917
00:52:36,904 --> 00:52:39,407
People are no longer
interested in perfection.

918
00:52:39,949 --> 00:52:41,450
What they need to see

919
00:52:41,868 --> 00:52:43,202
is authenticity.

920
00:52:44,787 --> 00:52:45,788
And trust me.

921
00:52:47,331 --> 00:52:48,666
Your family…

922
00:52:49,041 --> 00:52:51,043
is very, very marketable.

923
00:52:54,213 --> 00:52:58,175
Thank you, Mr. Salvador, for your time.

924
00:53:08,394 --> 00:53:10,521
-Enzo.
-Ms. D.

925
00:53:11,188 --> 00:53:15,109
Find out everything
about that Ricardo Salvador.

926
00:53:16,110 --> 00:53:18,487
Check if his credentials are real.

927
00:53:21,657 --> 00:53:23,492
I'd like to know…

928
00:53:24,869 --> 00:53:30,333
why he would be
so interested in this mess.

929
00:53:49,268 --> 00:53:50,686
What are you waiting for?

930
00:53:53,356 --> 00:53:56,192
Cala Soda just dropped to number two.

931
00:53:57,860 --> 00:54:00,696
It's the first time in years.

932
00:54:00,780 --> 00:54:01,614
What?

933
00:54:05,826 --> 00:54:09,038
Our distributors canceled their orders.

934
00:54:09,497 --> 00:54:13,334
Grocery stores and convenience stores

935
00:54:13,417 --> 00:54:15,461
are losing sales.

936
00:54:15,544 --> 00:54:19,173
Also, there's an increasing call
on social media

937
00:54:19,256 --> 00:54:22,009
for consumers to boycott our products.

938
00:54:22,635 --> 00:54:26,013
-Shut up! Get out!
-Okay, ma'am.

939
00:54:37,817 --> 00:54:40,152
Ms. D, the background check is complete.

940
00:54:40,653 --> 00:54:41,487
Proceed.

941
00:54:44,448 --> 00:54:45,574
Ricardo Salvador.

942
00:54:45,658 --> 00:54:48,577
He studied at a top-notch university
in Indonesia,

943
00:54:48,661 --> 00:54:50,746
and graduated at the top of his class.

944
00:54:50,830 --> 00:54:53,207
He's also a Silver Graph
Awards Hall of Famer.

945
00:54:53,958 --> 00:54:55,543
He was telling the truth.

946
00:54:55,626 --> 00:54:58,713
He is known
as one of the best crisis doctors.

947
00:54:59,380 --> 00:55:01,632
For instance, a politician from Indonesia

948
00:55:01,716 --> 00:55:04,260
who was involved
in a major corruption scandal

949
00:55:04,927 --> 00:55:06,429
got reelected with his help.

950
00:55:06,804 --> 00:55:08,848
He also turned
a tech company's data breach

951
00:55:08,931 --> 00:55:11,350
into an innovation story.

952
00:55:11,684 --> 00:55:14,311
And he changed the image of a celebrity

953
00:55:14,395 --> 00:55:17,565
accused of drug abuse to a survivor.

954
00:55:18,524 --> 00:55:21,444
He's an expert in manipulating
public perception, Ms. D.

955
00:55:21,986 --> 00:55:23,779
Why did he go back to the Philippines?

956
00:55:23,863 --> 00:55:25,948
He wanted to do his own thing.

957
00:55:26,657 --> 00:55:28,409
He's establishing his practice here.

958
00:55:30,953 --> 00:55:32,872
Set a meeting with him.

959
00:55:36,834 --> 00:55:40,296
You stole my husband!
You deserve more than this!

960
00:55:43,090 --> 00:55:43,966
Cut!

961
00:55:44,800 --> 00:55:46,093
Good take!

962
00:55:46,177 --> 00:55:47,803
-Okay. Reset.
-Are you okay? Okay.

963
00:55:47,887 --> 00:55:49,597
We'll shoot at a different angle
to be sure.

964
00:55:49,680 --> 00:55:50,890
I have to submerge my face in water again?

965
00:55:51,432 --> 00:55:52,308
-You're the body double, right?
-Yes.

966
00:55:53,184 --> 00:55:54,560
Have the makeup department fix your look

967
00:55:54,643 --> 00:55:56,353
-to ensure continuity.
-Okay.

968
00:55:56,437 --> 00:55:58,064
-Kaori, just keep it up.
-Okay.

969
00:55:58,147 --> 00:56:00,983
-Safety first, right?
-Of course. I know.

970
00:56:01,067 --> 00:56:02,318
-Just add more intensity.
-I love my life.

971
00:56:02,401 --> 00:56:03,527
-Are you okay?
-Okay.

972
00:56:03,611 --> 00:56:04,904
-Andi, come here.
-Sit down first.

973
00:56:04,987 --> 00:56:06,322
Take care.

974
00:56:07,073 --> 00:56:09,867
Make it more intense, okay?

975
00:56:09,950 --> 00:56:11,994
Can you try this? Are you okay with…

976
00:56:17,541 --> 00:56:18,751
Patricia.

977
00:56:20,294 --> 00:56:21,378
Sir.

978
00:56:22,338 --> 00:56:25,007
I'm flattered that you know my name.

979
00:56:25,091 --> 00:56:26,675
Are you the producer?

980
00:56:28,427 --> 00:56:29,762
No.

981
00:56:29,845 --> 00:56:31,514
I'm Ricardo Salvador.

982
00:56:32,556 --> 00:56:34,683
I'm La Familia's new PR specialist.

983
00:56:38,104 --> 00:56:39,688
I have an offer for you.

984
00:56:40,397 --> 00:56:41,982
I just need your cooperation.

985
00:56:42,483 --> 00:56:43,859
I don't want to have
any connection with my mom

986
00:56:43,943 --> 00:56:45,486
and you expect me to cooperate?

987
00:56:45,569 --> 00:56:47,154
You're drowning in debt.

988
00:56:50,908 --> 00:56:54,745
You need money
to settle your father's mess.

989
00:56:55,788 --> 00:56:59,750
We'll pay you so you can start over.

990
00:57:05,381 --> 00:57:07,174
I take it that it comes at a cost.

991
00:57:07,508 --> 00:57:09,802
Just like everything else in life.

992
00:57:09,885 --> 00:57:11,554
But I can assure you one thing.

993
00:57:11,887 --> 00:57:13,180
It'll be easier than doing all this.

994
00:57:15,307 --> 00:57:16,725
Here's my calling card.

995
00:57:17,726 --> 00:57:18,853
Think about it.

996
00:57:21,647 --> 00:57:23,315
It's the perfect role for you.

997
00:57:57,683 --> 00:58:01,020
What's the real story

998
00:58:01,103 --> 00:58:04,023
behind one of the country's
richest families?

999
00:58:04,523 --> 00:58:05,900
According to an initial report,

1000
00:58:05,983 --> 00:58:07,401
Diana Aragon suffered a heart attack

1001
00:58:07,484 --> 00:58:09,737
after there was
a reported issue of food poisoning

1002
00:58:09,820 --> 00:58:11,488
in one of their feeding programs.

1003
00:58:11,572 --> 00:58:13,282
-You deserve more than this!
-Take this!

1004
00:58:14,283 --> 00:58:16,118
-Dad!
-Dad!

1005
00:58:16,202 --> 00:58:17,620
-Ah!
-Ah!

1006
00:58:19,121 --> 00:58:20,539
Get out of here!

1007
00:58:21,290 --> 00:58:23,584
For the first time ever,

1008
00:58:23,667 --> 00:58:25,586
the mother and daughter
everyone is talking about

1009
00:58:25,669 --> 00:58:28,130
will face each other.

1010
00:58:28,797 --> 00:58:30,507
This Sunday,

1011
00:58:30,591 --> 00:58:33,135
let's break the silence.

1012
00:58:33,219 --> 00:58:36,430
It's the exclusive interview
everyone is waiting for.

1013
00:58:36,513 --> 00:58:38,182
Diana Aragon.

1014
00:58:38,265 --> 00:58:40,601
Patricia Aragon Dela Cruz.

1015
00:58:41,018 --> 00:58:42,144
Mother and daughter.

1016
00:58:42,228 --> 00:58:44,438
They will face and confront each other

1017
00:58:44,521 --> 00:58:46,357
in a tell-all interview.

1018
00:58:46,440 --> 00:58:48,901
This Sunday on…

1019
00:58:48,984 --> 00:58:50,194
Uncovered!

1020
00:58:57,409 --> 00:58:59,620
Ms. D? Patricia?

1021
00:58:59,703 --> 00:59:01,121
The interview is about to start.

1022
00:59:01,205 --> 00:59:02,331
Coming.

1023
00:59:03,749 --> 00:59:05,251
All good now, Ms. D.

1024
00:59:20,724 --> 00:59:21,809
She's still an Aragon.

1025
00:59:21,892 --> 00:59:22,977
I have to keep an eye on her.

1026
00:59:23,060 --> 00:59:24,979
I have it from good sources

1027
00:59:25,062 --> 00:59:27,773
that Patricia will be working
at La Familia.

1028
00:59:27,856 --> 00:59:30,317
Working at La Familia
wasn't part of the deal.

1029
00:59:30,401 --> 00:59:31,694
It's not just Diana
who'll benefit from this.

1030
00:59:31,777 --> 00:59:34,113
It will also change your life.

1031
00:59:34,196 --> 00:59:35,656
-No excuses.
-Ah!

1032
00:59:35,739 --> 00:59:36,657
-Can you handle it?
-Of course.

1033
00:59:36,740 --> 00:59:40,202
Why are you meddling with something
that's not within your scope of work?

1034
00:59:40,286 --> 00:59:41,620
Why are you yelling at my daughter?

1035
00:59:41,704 --> 00:59:43,706
I'm scolding her
because she did something wrong.

1036
00:59:43,789 --> 00:59:46,333
Just admit that you're mad at Patricia.

1037
00:59:46,417 --> 00:59:48,460
You still see me that way even until now?
